@startuml rules_classes
title Class rules (tp::rules): may a tractor compete in a pulling class?
hide empty members
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "tp::rules" {
  class ClassRules <<struct>> {
    +max_mass_kg : double
    +max_pto_power_w : double
    +max_engine_speed_rad_s : double
    +max_hitch_height_m : double
  }
  class Compliance <<struct>> {
    +too_heavy : bool
    +too_much_pto_power : bool
    +engine_speed_too_high : bool
    +hitch_too_high : bool
    +hitch_above_rear_axle : bool
    +ok() : bool
  }
  enum ParamError {
    kNotFinite
    kLimitNotPositive
  }
  class "rules functions" as RulesFns <<free functions>> {
    +validate(const ClassRules&) : optional<ParamError>
    +pto_power_w(const vehicle::Params&) : double
    +check(const ClassRules&, const vehicle::Params&) : Compliance
  }
  RulesFns ..> ClassRules
  RulesFns ..> Compliance
  RulesFns ..> ParamError
}

package "tp::vehicle / tp::engine" {
  class "vehicle::Params\n+ pto_efficiency" as Tractor <<struct>>
  class "engine::max_net_power_w()" as EnginePower <<free function>>
}

RulesFns ..> Tractor : reads mass, hitch,\nhigh idle, PTO efficiency
RulesFns ..> EnginePower : PTO power =\nnet peak × PTO efficiency
note bottom of ClassRules
  competition rules, not physics: loaded from data/classes/,
  checked at setup (never in the step); upgrades change
  tractor parameters, which must stay within the class
end note
@enduml
